{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/885521-question-about-the-egyptian-pantheon","id":885521,"title":"Question About The Egyptian Pantheon.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-08T11:33:20-07:00","id":885521,"title":"Question About The Egyptian Pantheon.","content":"if the pantheon as whole are called Netjer,and the highest deities are called Pesedjet. then,what is the Ennead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T11:40:26-07:00","id":885532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/885521-question-about-the-egyptian-pantheon#post885521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if the pantheon as whole are called Netjer,and the highest deities are called Pesedjet. then,what is the Ennead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ennead is pretty much the more common Greek term for the Pesedjet. Like how the Greek name &quot;Osiris&quot; is more commonly used than Azar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-08-2016, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T11:42:02-07:00","id":885533,"title":"","content":"Oh,so. The gods in ScionVerse dont use the world because its greek?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T11:50:20-07:00","id":885542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/885521-question-about-the-egyptian-pantheon?p=885533#post885533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh,so. The gods in ScionVerse dont use the world because its greek?</div> </div> </div> </div>They might use it too *shrugs*. 1E used the Greek names for most of the gods in the Egyptian Pnatheon as primary.<br /> <br /> But it is not a native Egyptian term, no. It's Greek for &quot;set of nine&quot;, referring to the nine primary deities of Heliopolis (Ra, Tefnut, Shu, Nut, Geb, Isis, Osiris, Nephthys, and Set). Things get a bit complicated for Scion because something like 3 or 4 of those deities are actually Titans, and via later developments in Egyptian myth, you can't exclude the likes of Horus, Thoth, Ptah, Hathor/Sekhmet, etc as Greater Deities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T12:35:37-07:00","id":885590,"title":"","content":"Ra and Atum (the guy who raised from the sea and created everything) are the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T12:46:11-07:00","id":885603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/885521-question-about-the-egyptian-pantheon?p=885590#post885590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ra and Atum (the guy who raised from the sea and created everything) are the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ra and Atum were increasingly conflated through history as the cult of Ra ascended and subsumed earlier myths. I have no inside knowledge on this topic, but my GUESS is that in Scion, Atum is a Titan that Ra conquered and claimed his Ren (Name) in victory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:51:19-07:00","id":885660,"title":"","content":"It's a little more the other way. Atum, the ram headed dude, was the tutelary deity of the nome which contained Thebes. After a dynasty shift brought a Theban family to the throne and the Pharaoh (which was the palace and center of government as much as the person inside it. Sort of like calling the President of the USA &quot;the White House) to their nome, Ra, as supreme deity, was conflated with their patron. Which was not uncommon (there's Horus-Ra, etc. Who is the same, but different from Horus/Heru. Who is the same but different from Heru-er. Who is the same, but different from Re-Horkhaty. Etc.) but ends up being problematic for the purposes of a game. A lot of the specific nomes also had specific myths associated with &quot;their&quot; gods, which were sometimes at odds with what we consider the &quot;core mythology&quot;. So... Ra created the world thusly, Ptah created it thusly, Atum created it thusly, Khephreh created it thusly, etc., etc. All completely mutually exclusively, of course. You get that when you are talking about thousands of years of mythology written down over what amounts to a very large area considering the transportation technology of the time. <br /> <br /> If you were going to try to make a coherent Scion-ish linear story-path, the best card toss in the hat I've got would probably be to have Ra be the Titan. Have the &quot;generational conflict&quot; between the &quot;titans&quot; and the gods have been solved by Isis when she stole his power, leaving hims a senile mess and then Atum somehow getting ahold of the rest and doing something to make that-which-was-Atum and that-which-was-Ra into Atum-Ra. NOT, mind you by eating him. That was about the ultimate no-no. <br /> <br /> And using all the transliterations of the names in Egyptian, instead of the more common Greek ones, would lose what familiarity people have with the Egyptian gods/Netjer. A lot more people know who Anubis is compared to Anpu. Isis' name recognition has gone sideways recently, but it's still more associated with an Egyptian goddess to most people than Ese. Oh, and, of course, one can get into the ENDLESS arguments about even those names, pronunciations, etc. Particularly over the vast range of time mentioned above. Yada, yada, yada.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:24:24-07:00","id":885702,"title":"","content":"Ajax, I believe you are thinking of Amun, and his conflation with Ra. That happened with the political ascent of Thebes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T15:55:17-07:00","id":885748,"title":"","content":"Ouch. Yeah.... Shows what happens when I don't cross-check with Budge.... Too lazy to walk the ten steps to my office today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T15:59:44-07:00","id":885754,"title":"","content":"Neall said it was possible that Ra was a Titan forced to be part of the pantheon by Isis.<br /> Damn,isis sort of mean wast she?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":