man known simply as The Emperor has been alive for over 10,000 years. The military took to worshiping him as some sort of God and are <b><i>extremely intolerant</i></b> towards any ideas that contradict this belief. They're also supremacists and believe all alien races are vile scum compared to humanity, so they seek to exterminate them and expand their empire across the galaxy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pretty much the Roman Empire in a sci-fi setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T21:32:37-07:00","id":886954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/885521-question-about-the-egyptian-pantheon?p=886947#post886947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To clarify, by the way, Warhammer takes place in the distant future where some human known simply as The Emperor has been alive for over 10,000 years. The military took to worshiping him as some sort of God and are <b><i>extremely intolerant</i></b> towards any ideas that contradict this belief. They're also supremacists and believe all alien races are vile scum compared to humanity, so they seek to exterminate them and expand their empire across the galaxy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pretty much the Roman Empire in a sci-fi setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... Except for the systemic genocide and caring about religious contradiction. Those aren't very Roman. Rome generally just imposed its gods in addition to any native gods. Only Judea really ever had a problem with that specifically. They also tried to suppress Christians for trying to convert people away from the Roman gods, but if the Christians had just been a henotheisitic mystery cult like Mithraeists or the Isis Cult, them recruiting probably wouldn't have been a problem for Imperial authorities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T21:39:58-07:00","id":886955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/885521-question-about-the-egyptian-pantheon?p=886954#post886954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well... Except for the systemic genocide and caring about religious contradiction. Those aren't very Roman. Rome generally just imposed its gods in addition to any native gods. Only Judea really ever had a problem with that specifically. They also tried to suppress Christians for trying to convert people away from the Roman gods, but if the Christians had just been a henotheisitic mystery cult like Mithraeists or the Isis Cult, them recruiting probably wouldn't have been a problem for Imperial authorities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh. I knew that Rome absorbed the groups it conquered, but I didn't know it was that tolerant about religious diversity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T21:54:50-07:00","id":886963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/885521-question-about-the-egyptian-pantheon?p=886955#post886955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Huh. I knew that Rome absorbed the groups it conquered, but I didn't know it was that tolerant about religious diversity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Empire usually didn't care as long as you paid your taxes and weren't trying to convert people AWAY from the Roman gods. Convenient thing about polytheism is there isn't a limit on gods you can accept.<br /> <br /> I mean, they did kill a lot of Druids, but that was more political than religious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T04:30:13-07:00","id":887072,"title":"","content":"There was also the old &quot;You worship our gods already, you just call them different names&quot; shtick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T05:12:44-07:00","id":887083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/885521-question-about-the-egyptian-pantheon?p=887072#post887072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was also the old &amp;quot;You worship our gods already, you just call them different names&amp;quot; shtick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think when it comes to Scion,when that happens the gods may absorb each other' mantle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:46:29-07:00","id":887213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/885521-question-about-the-egyptian-pantheon?p=886963#post886963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Empire usually didn't care as long as you paid your taxes and weren't trying to convert people AWAY from the Roman gods. Convenient thing about polytheism is there isn't a limit on gods you can accept.<br /> <br /> I mean, they did kill a lot of Druids, but that was more political than religious.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did have to worship the Imperial Cult (the deified and, later, current emperors). Other than that, the Romans (until that Christianity thing) WANTED you to worship the &quot;gods of your fathers&quot;. <br /> <br /> Except, yes, for the Gauls and then, later, the Britons. As they, like the Jews, were using their religion as a rallying point for anti-Imperial sentiments. Plus, ya know, the Romans always had a lingering fear of the Gauls (and their druids) after the whole sacking of Rome thing....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reac